  "details": "As the localization refactor works suggested, I did some review about merged strings, and here is my suggestion for splitting them. \n\n- General/Avatars : Split into UI and tooltip string, which can be translate for MM/Avatar as \"User avatars, double click to open avatar world search\".\n\n- General/Behavior :Their are two usage, report user behavior and camera behavior.\n\n- General/Environment: Camera filter environments and reporting a social environment.\n\n- General/Block_User : Split into UI and tooltip string, for example, if you block a user, he/she will not longer visiable and also can not search you with global user search.  for transmits more useful info about these moderation functions to the end user.\n\n- General/Kick_User : Same as above.\n\n- General/Warn_User : Same as above. \n\n- General/Safety : Split into UI and tooltip string, \"You can change your safety level here\"... flexibility for localization. \n\n- General/View_Avatar_Author : Split into UI and tooltip string, for example: \"The avatar author, click to view additional infomation about this user.\"\n\n- General/View_Avatar_Details : Same as above. \n\n- General/LOD_Quality : Same as above, split it into ui and tooltip string, to transmit more details to the end user, for example : High LOD can be helping with better visual experience, but, might be increase CPU usage.\n\n- General/Convert_Dynamic_Bones_to_PhysBones : split it into ui and tooltip string, \"it may be help with performance, but might result some weird issue in specific 2.0 avatars. This function toggle is local only.\"\n\n- General/New : I wish it can split again as before, which should be use as : new notification, latest official news, etc.\n\nAlso, here are some thing I suggest to split as UI & Tooltip which can provide flexibility for localization. It's not so necessary but if they want to, it's really very fun.\n\n- General/Backflip (I really want to translate it as: show me a backflip! )\n\n- General/Cheer  (Same as above)\n\n- General/Clap\n\n- General/Dance\n\n- General/Die\n\n- General/Point\n\n- General/Sadness\n\n- General/Wave\n\n- General/Thank_You_For_Supporting_VRChat ( Recently, we did translate the vrcat one as \"thank you supporting VRChat, meow! \" so pls bring it back.)",
